Well, I'm tempted to say it's just bad luck.  But such is not the case.
Unbeknownst to most people (even the Dev Team :) there was a secret flag
added called NEWPLAYER.  Ever stare in awe at those other postings about
god-like characters with tons of really cool stuff?  Ever wonder why you
never can find any of that stuff, or get more than a half-dozen levels
into the dungeon?  NEWPLAYER is the reason!

That's right.  NEWPLAYER is a flag which keeps track of the number of games
a particular person has played.  Until this number exceeds some random
number (anywhere from a dozen to several hundred games), don't expect to
find any cool items or make it too far.  In fact, if the game thinks you're
doing too good, it will try to kill you in some devious way.  Some examples:

* Sending in a horde of orcs far before you're capable of handling them.
* Sticking a floating eye in a hallway you happen to be running through.
* Level-teleporting you a couple dozen levels down.
* Making sure that that random potion you quaff at a vulnerable time is a
  bad one, e.g. blindness or paralysis.
* Placing a nice powerful tower of flame underneath that big pile of gold.

So in short, the only way to get around the NEWPLAYER flag is to get your-
self addicted to nethack and to play _lots_ of games.  But try not to get
TOO addicted; the game also senses when you've become successful, and when
enough people have gotten powerful characters, email messages are sent to
the Dev Team letting them know it's time to release another non-backwards-
compatible patch.

